  "methods": [
    "Build 3 owner rule dated 2026-10-29: clear only original build 1 held rows outside excluded territories with name contradiction a together with b or c; name-matching bc-only rows remain held. Names fold case, accents, punctuation and conservative generic edge terms including native labels/aliases/P1705. Settlement points fail only when every current Earth point is more than 10 km away; administrative units require official boundary exclusion. Complete current P131 graph must fail to reach the expected state, or current P17 excludes the expected country. Unknown evidence is not a failed test. No replacement item assigned. Build 1 proved owners and all six changes preserved.",
    "Owner decision 2026-10-29: name contradiction a plus b or c; unknown is not failed. Generic name normalization is conservative; administrative point distance alone never proves exclusion. Current archived best-rank statements only.",
    "Each row independently tested by exact Unicode NFC casefold label/alias, best-rank current Earth P625 <=10km, unique P17 country, explicit current P131 path to pinned state, direct compatible P31 and independent official code/name/state/scope binding. Unit ownership additionally has e-Stat polygon containment for both row and item points. Clears require positive distinct-entity proof, not a failed ownership gate. New item additionally preserves the original v4.0 key name/native/state/country/point/type and passes the same ownership gates. No shared identifier proves ownership. Unproved items and special/disputed cases are held unchanged."
